Makefile                                   make dev also builds the packer, for In-Game Reset's apploader.img; verifies and extracts the pinned libiconv-lite overlay before compiling, while keeping the SDK's pre-installed TinySMB and libuchardet; copies the whitespace-normalized docs/licenses/lwip.txt so host packaging checks need no SDK mount
cube/packer/Makefile                       compresses with xz: the build image has no 7z; links its files in byte order, whatever the locale
cube/swiss/include/bba.h                 first-launch release checks may initialize the network for outbound traffic alone; existing network callers retain their services
cube/swiss/Makefile                        tags.h is empty (its reader, load_auto_dol, never runs in Indigo); links its files in byte order, names the commit in exactly 7 characters and no build path, so the DOL is the same in any locale, clone and folder; UI_PERF=1 builds the performance overlay; UI_540P=1 links the isolated experimental VIDEO driver; no unwind tables, which nothing reads, and -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti on C++; AESND is built from cube/swiss/aesnd, not -laesnd; TinySMB (-ltinysmb) and libuchardet stay in place of upstream's libsmb2 and uchardet-lite; libiconv-lite overlay precedes the SDK portlibs; cold application code uses -Os/LTO in one partition while the hot background, Jewel Case, font and audio objects retain their audited -O2/non-LTO policy; exception frames remain while their unused index is omitted; upstream sntp.c is not compiled because Indigo retains its opt-in bounded client; emits per-function stack usage (.su) for CI's static frame ceiling check
